This directory records the provenance of the 55 DifferentialGeometry Lean
sources used by the local chart connection proof.

The originals are from qinz1yang/differential-geometry at
8bd406e35c33a200e9b88895cf11ee8429194e15 and are released under the Apache
License 2.0. LICENSE and README.upstream.md are copied from that commit.
Contributor notices remain in the sources, including Jack McCarthy and
Ziyang Qin notices. The upstream README describes its historical setup;
the present package uses official Lean 4.33.0 and Mathlib
db584cd6d46c92f209a44c0f1c829460d327499d.

The port changes 26 upstream files for those APIs. Definitions and statements
are not all preserved literally. The actual chartLeviCivita,
chartLeviCivitaInnerCLM and chartLeviCivitaGoodSet definitions match the
original source text after newline normalization. SOURCE-PROVENANCE.json
records every original and ported source hash and the import graph.
minimal-upstream-port.patch retains the reviewed source delta.
MetricCompatible retains its original ChartDensity import, and Section
retains its original Mathlib.Geometry.Manifold.Algebra.SmoothFunctions import.

ChartPort/MetricAPI.lean and ChartPort/ChartIdentity.lean are new local work.
They reuse the project's existing RicciFlow.SmoothForward.toC2 and chosen
Levi-Civita connection. The comparison uses the upstream chart construction,
its proved torsion and metric compatibility, local Koszul uniqueness and a
smooth section through a tangent vector. It applies to the constant downgraded
family, points in the actual chart good set and sections differentiable at
the evaluation point. Its finite-dimensional complete real tangent model,
smooth manifold, T2Space and SigmaCompactSpace premises are retained.

The 13 inherited project modules remain the exact public base files. Twelve
earlier desktop copies differ only by CRLF/LF encoding; those evidence bytes
remain historical and do not replace the public files. The 31 Mathlib support
sources are unchanged pinned originals addressing missing artifacts; they
are not vendored here or modified in the Mathlib package.

The mathematical proof packet has independent review approval. This concrete
candidate has not yet been compiled or qualified by its proposed focused CI.
Copied development imports and prior receipts do not qualify a new candidate.
Historical source binding and full master inventory admission remain pending.
Point4 and both general targets remain OPEN. Global chart coverage,
evolving-family comparison, upstream global chosen-connection equality,
curvature and Ricci comparisons, and PDE existence remain separate work.
